## Lore

Also known as "Loaders" or "Moes" ' || char(8212) || ' short for munitions experts ' || char(8212) || ' each member of
the three or four man Reload Team is a combination munitions and explosives
expert and assistant Operator. They are used only in the Quebec Army and
specialise in power armor mechanics, weapon systems and explosives with an
emphasis on Glitter Boy systems.

Moes are trained to ignore the danger and chaos around them and stay focused on
the task at hand: typically reloading and maintaining one to ten Glitter Boys
under combat conditions. The primary mission is to keep their Glitter Boys
fighting ' || char(8212) || ' reloading ammunition as fast as possible, making weapon adjustments
and modifications, bypassing damage, jury-rigging weapon systems and making
whatever field repairs are needed.

Most have extraordinary Mental Endurance, and are dedicated, driven and
fearless. Although the first priority is to load and maintain Glitter Boys of
all types ' || char(8212) || ' the Classic and the Taurus especially depend on them ' || char(8212) || ' Loaders are
combat trained soldiers who will not hesitate to fight. Unless ordered
otherwise, they fight to defend the Glitter Boy they are assigned to. If that
Glitter Boy is destroyed they rescue the pilot and either return to base camp
for reassignment or "adopt" another one, several if circumstances require it.

## GM Notes

The team''s RHV-60 Reloader Hover Vehicle seats four and has a large covered or
open-air cargo bay holding ammo-drums, mortar shells, munitions and power packs
as well as tools and replacement parts. Magnetic clamps and straps carry a
back-up GB big gun. It resembles a long, flat hovercycle or a hover pick-up
truck; the four man team sits in the open so they never have to leave the
platform to work, and it is fitted out as a mechanic''s work station with a small
crane and a hydraulics system. Diagnostic equipment, optical enhancements and
sensory equipment are part of the vehicle rather than the character''s kit.

Equipment available upon assignment: fusion blocks, plastique and additional
explosives, EOD equipment and other munitions, heavy weapons, tools and
equipment, depending on the mission, the commanding officer and availability.

The soldier''s quarters is a dormitory shared by the four teammates, each with a
private bedroom and study, CD stereo, television and VCD, mini-refrigerator,
desk, dresser and a comfortable bed.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fq-gb-reloader');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fq-gb-reloader';

